From 634e18e14690582766f77695392df366f301e064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: go-while <go-while@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:48:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configure: Don't warn about C11 constructs with Clang

With its C23 interfaces enabled, glibc 2.43 implements strchr, strrchr,
strstr, memchr and a few other string functions as macros using
_Generic, so that they return a const pointer for a const argument.
Clang's -Wpre-c11-compat, part of -Weverything, flags every call that
expands such a macro, and make warnings fails on the first one
(lib/artnumber.c on Ubuntu 26.04).

Disable that warning for Clang.  This turns it off for all code built
with Clang, not only for these macros.  GCC's -Wc99-c11-compat stays,
so GCC builds still check INN's own code for C11 constructs; GCC does
not warn about the macros, which come from a system header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 configure.ac | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index cdaf5f7e6..dc184b2ef 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -808,6 +808,7 @@ dnl   -Wnrvo                          Fine in C.
 dnl   -Wpacked                        Not an actual problem.
 dnl   -Wpadded                        Not an actual problem.
 dnl   -Wpoison-system-directories     Not an actual problem (e.g. Xcode).
+dnl   -Wpre-c11-compat                glibc 2.43 string.h macros use _Generic.
 dnl   -Wreserved-id-macro             Autoconf sets several of these normally.
 dnl   -Wreserved-identifier           False positives with FD_ZERO.
 dnl   -Wsign-conversion               Too many fiddly changes for the benefit.
@@ -854,7 +855,7 @@ m4_foreach_w(
      -Wno-disabled-macro-expansion -Wno-excess-padding -Wno-extra-semi-stmt
      -Wno-implicit-int-conversion -Wno-implicit-void-ptr-cast
      -Wno-packed -Wno-padded
-     -Wno-poison-system-directories
+     -Wno-poison-system-directories -Wno-pre-c11-compat
      -Wno-reserved-id-macro -Wno-reserved-identifier -Wno-shorten-64-to-32
      -Wno-sign-conversion -Wno-stack-protector-purecap-ignored
      -Wno-switch-default -Wno-switch-enum
-- 
2.47.3

